<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela congress approves Orinoco oil partners.</title>
<headline>Venezuela congress approves Orinoco oil partners.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's congress gave its final approval Thursday to the addition of Norway's Den Norske Stats Oljeselskap A/S (Statoil) and Norsk Hydro to a heavy oil joint venture involving state oil subsidiary Maraven and France's Total, legislators said.</p>
<p>The project, which was approved by Congress in 1993, originally included Japan's Itochu and Marubeni, but those companies pulled out last year.  </p>
<p>The $5 billion project envisages 200,000 barrels per day (bpd) of heavy crude production from the Zuata region of the Orinocco Oil belt. It includes construction of a new deep conversion facility on the Caribbean coast which will export about 175,000 bpd of light sweet crude, due to come onstream in 2002.</p>
<p>((-- John Paul Rathbone, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
